<!--Post: 13172--><!--Time: 1114452945-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13172"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 11:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->WICHITA, Kansas, 2005423 -- In it, Rader writes: <BR> <BR>     Dear congregation, <BR> <BR>     Thank you for recent cards, letters and prayers. I want you all to know that Pastor Clark is indeed a good shepherd. <BR> <BR>     There are many things that I would like to tell you at this time but I must be careful with attorney-client relationship. We are working at it one step at a time. <BR> <BR>     Then, off to the side, Rader writes, &#34;When in Rome do as the Roman.&#34; <BR> <BR>     The letter resumes, saying: <BR> <BR>     The judicial system is treating me with respect and care. Food is not too bad. Have a good Christian Easter. <BR> <BR>     Sincerely in Christ, Dennis L. Rader. <BR> <BR>     Last update: Apr 25, 2005, 8:02am  <BR>See more stories by Jason Kravarik  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13172-->
<!--Post: 13191--><!--Time: 1114524745-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13191"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 7:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hope his church realized this letter is a facade! What a hypocrite! Jesus is going to punch him in the head. Right Johno?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13191-->
<!--Post: 13197--><!--Time: 1114526961-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13197"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 7:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Jesus is going to punch him in the head.&#34; <BR> <BR>Why do I find that so funny? It should be on a bumper sticker.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13197-->
<!--Post: 13199--><!--Time: 1114527272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13199"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 7:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is that letter a direct translation of what he wrote? If it is, he is producing work in direct opposition and quality to the other letter posted. Yes, he knows what to say and to whom. He plays each role separately and is not able to integrate into one person. He is the good husband/father, the good church member, the able code enforcer, and an outstanding serial killer. That will never change. He is very fragmented. It would be interesting to assess his abstract thinking. He is very concrete, and as long as he can take a &#39;hands on&#39; approach to whatever he is doing, he excells: ADT schematics, knot tying, measuring the grass. Can you imagine how that would bore the rest of us? One could not do that for long without having to move on. That is why retarded persons work so well on assembly lines. They do not get bored as easily, and they are grateful for the job. Of course, administering testing to him could benefit the defense as well as put them in jeopardy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13199-->
<!--Post: 13200--><!--Time: 1114530561-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13200"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 8:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good points Tear Drop. <BR>The &#34;note&#34; indicates a person who could possibly have dyslexia and/or be mentally &#34;challenged.&#34; <BR>However, as you said, the letter to his church congregation relects a stable god loving and fearing, let alone caring individual. <BR>Unless, of course, the letter to his congregation was edited. <BR>The &#34;note&#34; and the &#34;letter&#34; reflect two different individuals. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13200-->
<!--Post: 13201--><!--Time: 1114530635-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13201"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 8:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When was this letter written? It&#39;s over a month since Easter.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13201-->
<!--Post: 13206--><!--Time: 1114537441-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13206"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 10:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Stevey: Johno gets the props and coined that phrase under another thread. I thought it was funny too! According to Johno, Jesus despised hypocrites and would have punched DTDC in the head.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13206-->
<!--Post: 13209--><!--Time: 1114539292-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 11:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was furious when I read Denny The Dog Catchers&#39; latest letter to his church, above. The last part &#34;Have a good Christian Easter. Sincerely in Christ, Dennis L. Rader.&#34; should have included the following; <BR>  <BR>  &#34;Sincerely in Christ- Except when I&#39;m out stalking, kidnapping, torturing &amp; murdering Gods&#39; children. And taunting all of his good followers about it for my whole life with packages &amp; letters reminding everyone that I did it &amp; would love to do it again. Sincerely, DTDC.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13209-->
<!--Post: 13213--><!--Time: 1114549661-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13213"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 2:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>The &#34;note&#34; and the &#34;letter&#34; reflect two different individuals</i> <BR> <BR>The up side is that, since &#39;Bad Denny&#39; seems to show no remorse for his deeds, having &#39;Good Denny&#39; joined at the hip will at least acertain that the guilty central nervous system feels the effects of his heretofore interminable incarceration. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13213-->
<!--Post: 13215--><!--Time: 1114550772-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13215"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 2:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thou shall not kill, Thou shall not kill, Thou shall not kill, you demon @&#42;&#42;! Sincerely in Christ! Give me a break! If Jesus doesn&#39;t punch you in the head I&#39;m going to you freak! <BR> <BR>Sorry guys, I&#39;m venting. This in infuriates me!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13215-->
<!--Post: 13217--><!--Time: 1114552595-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13217"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 2:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What would Jesus do? <BR>Jesus would have decked him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13217-->
<!--Post: 13223--><!--Time: 1114573919-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13223"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule: You&#39;re giving DTDC too much credit. You are assuming that the slimes&#39; &#39;good side&#39; will make him feel &#34;guilty&#34;- not at all. If that was so, he would have killed himself several decades ago.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13223-->
<!--Post: 13243--><!--Time: 1114642494-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13243"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 3:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pardon my sloppy wording. I didn&#39;t mean to infer that he would feel &#39;guilty&#39;. I meant to say that a part of him would be aware of his incarceration &#40;as opposed to the part of him that would sit in a closet for hours waiting for a victim&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13243-->
<!--Post: 13245--><!--Time: 1114644146-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13245"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 4:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dennis Rader&#39;s desire to exert control and manipulation will continue until his life is extinguished. He can no longer derive gratification from murder, but can derive it from duping his congregation by emphasizing the facade of respectability.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13245-->
<!--Post: 13262--><!--Time: 1114702111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13262"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 8:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->His letter was all about &#39;me&#39;. He is incapable of feeling guilt. He has not one wit about what is being thought and speculated about the members of his church, his family, his parents, etc. He is all facade except when he is forcing the life out of someone. I wonder if his attorneys have nightmares about him. He is the embodiment of evil. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13262-->
<!--Post: 13267--><!--Time: 1114720955-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13267"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 28, 2005 - 1:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He is a pitiful excuse for a human being!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13267-->
